<policies>
  <!--
    The official lab's policy.xml (vendor/ai-gateway/labs/
    ai-foundry-hosted-agents-custom-framework/), unchanged, plus hop 2's
    gateway-measured timing left in API Management's built-in cache for hop 1 to
    pick up. The vendored file is never edited; this copy is what
    shared-apim-registration.bicep deploys. {backend-id} is substituted by
    upstream's inference-api.bicep, exactly as for the vendored file.

    Why: this hop's response goes to the agent's container, never to the broker,
    so its timing cannot travel back as response headers. The container does,
    however, carry the W3C trace of the request that invoked it (verified for
    pydantic-agent: every successful invocation's model call shares hop 1's
    trace id). Keyed by that trace id, hop 1's policy can read this hop's figures
    on its own way out and return them with the response.

    Measured exactly as hop 1 is (see hosted-agents-responses-policy.xml):
      backend  last inbound statement -> first outbound statement
      gateway  everything else up to the point the value is stored

    STREAMING CHANGES WHAT "backend" MEANS. Outbound runs when the model's
    response headers arrive. Both agents stream their model calls
    (ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog.IsStreamCompletion = true), so for them
    "backend" is the time to the first byte, not the model call's duration:
    measured 2026-09-24 at 2491 ms against the log's 3026 ms for 257 completion
    tokens, 8424 against 9414 for 950. Each entry therefore records whether the
    response was an event stream, and the broker never presents a streamed
    call's first-byte time as the model's duration. The gateway figure is
    unaffected in kind: it is APIM's own processing up to that point.

    Cache use on a gateway shared with other teams:
      - key prefix `hosted-agents-hop2:` plus a 128-bit random trace id, so it
        cannot collide with another team's key (they use response caching only);
      - caching-type="internal", explicitly: never an external cache someone
        else might attach later;
      - 120 s TTL, longer than the broker's 60 s invocation timeout and no longer;
      - a few dozen bytes per invocation.
    The built-in cache is volatile and its writes are asynchronous. A lost or
    late value is a cache miss, hop 1 returns no hop 2 headers, and the console
    falls back to the gateway log. It never produces a wrong figure, only a
    missing one.

    A request with no traceparent (strands-agent's model calls arrive without
    hop 1's trace) stores nothing.

    An agent can call the model more than once per invocation, so calls are
    appended as `gateway:backend:status:streamed;` (streamed is 1 or 0).
  -->
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <authentication-managed-identity resource="https://cognitiveservices.azure.com" output-token-variable-name="managed-id-access-token" ignore-error="false" />
    <set-header name="Authorization" exists-action="override">
      <value>@("Bearer " + (string)context.Variables["managed-id-access-token"])</value>
    </set-header>
    <set-backend-service backend-id="{backend-id}" />
    <set-variable name="hosted-agents-backend-start-ms" value="@(context.Elapsed.TotalMilliseconds)" />
  </inbound>
  <backend>
    <base />
  </backend>
  <outbound>
    <set-variable name="hosted-agents-backend-end-ms" value="@(context.Elapsed.TotalMilliseconds)" />
    <base />
    <set-variable name="hosted-agents-trace-id" value="@{
      var parts = context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("traceparent", "").Split('-');
      return (parts.Length == 4 && parts[1].Length == 32) ? parts[1].ToLowerInvariant() : "";
    }" />
    <choose>
      <when condition="@(((string)context.Variables["hosted-agents-trace-id"]).Length == 32)">
        <cache-lookup-value key="@("hosted-agents-hop2:" + (string)context.Variables["hosted-agents-trace-id"])" variable-name="hosted-agents-hop2-previous" default-value="" caching-type="internal" />
        <cache-store-value key="@("hosted-agents-hop2:" + (string)context.Variables["hosted-agents-trace-id"])" duration="120" caching-type="internal" value="@{
          var backend = (double)context.Variables["hosted-agents-backend-end-ms"] - (double)context.Variables["hosted-agents-backend-start-ms"];
          var gateway = context.Elapsed.TotalMilliseconds - backend;
          return (string)context.Variables["hosted-agents-hop2-previous"]
            + gateway.ToString("F1") + ":" + backend.ToString("F1") + ":" + context.Response.StatusCode
            + ":" + (context.Response.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("Content-Type", "").Contains("text/event-stream") ? "1" : "0") + ";";
        }" />
      </when>
    </choose>
  </outbound>
  <on-error>
    <base />
  </on-error>
</policies>
